<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Southcorp sells U.S. unit to Greif.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Southcorp sells U.S. unit to Greif.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southcorp Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday it planned to sell its North American steel drum business to Greif Brothers Inc based in Delaware, Ohio.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.  </p>
<p>Southcorp said its packaging division operated steel drum businesses in Merced, California, and in Oakville, Ontario.</p>
<p>Divisional executive general manager Barry Watts said the divestment was part of a larger strategy to focus Southcorp's North American packaging operations on its plastic packaging business based in Atlanta, Georgia.</p>
<p>Greif was conducting due diligence on the proposed acquisition, with a contract likely to be concluded soon.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
